  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>rms</keyword>
  <short_description>Root mean square value.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>Y = rms(X)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>Y = rms(X, DIM)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>Y = rms(X, VECDIM)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>Y = rms(X, "all")</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>Y = rms(..., TYPE)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>Y = rms(..., NANFLAG)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <param_input>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>X</param_name>
      <param_description>input data: single, double, logical or integer.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>DIM</param_name>
      <param_description>dimension to operate along.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>VECDIM</param_name>
      <param_description>vector of dimensions to operate along.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>"all"</param_name>
      <param_description>operate on every element of X.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>TYPE</param_name>
      <param_description>class of the result: "default", "double" or "native".</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>NANFLAG</param_name>
      <param_description>"includenan" or "omitnan". "includemissing" and "omitmissing" are also accepted.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
  </param_input>
  <param_output>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>Y</param_name>
      <param_description>root mean square values.</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
  </param_output>
  <description>
    <p><b>rms</b> computes sqrt(mean(abs(X) .^ 2)) along the selected dimension:</p>
    <latex>\mathrm{RMS}(X) = \sqrt{ \frac{1}{N} \sum_{n=1}^{N} |x_n|^2 }</latex>
    <p>where N is the number of elements along that dimension.</p>
    <p>
      <ul>
        <li>If <b>X</b> is a vector, <b>Y</b> is a scalar.</li>
        <li>If <b>X</b> is a matrix, <b>Y</b> is a row vector holding the value of each column.</li>
        <li>If <b>X</b> is a multidimensional array, <b>Y</b> is computed along the first dimension whose size is not 1, unless a dimension is given.</li>
      </ul>
    </p>
    <p><b>Class of the result:</b> the square and the mean always run in double, so an integer input never saturates. <b>"native"</b> returns the class of the input, <b>"double"</b> returns double, and <b>"default"</b> returns double for an integer input and the class of the input otherwise. A logical input is not an integer class and returns double.</p>
    <p><b>Missing values:</b> NaN values are included by default. Use <b>"omitnan"</b> or <b>"omitmissing"</b> to leave them out.</p>
  </description>
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description>root mean square of a vector</example_item_description>
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[
t = 0:0.001:1-0.001;
x = cos(2*pi*100*t);
y = rms(x)
% y = 0.7071
]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description>one value per column</example_item_description>
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[
x = [4 -5 1; 2 3 5; -9 1 7];
y = rms(x)
% y = [5.8023 3.4157 5.0000]
]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description>one value per row</example_item_description>
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[
x = [6 4 23 -3; 9 -10 4 11; 2 8 -5 1];
y = rms(x, 2)
% y = [12.1450; 8.9163; 4.8477]
]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description>leaving missing values out</example_item_description>
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[
x = [1.77 -0.005 nan -2.95; nan 0.34 nan 0.19];
y = rms(x, "omitnan")
% y = [1.7700 0.2404 nan 2.0903]
]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description>integer input with a native result</example_item_description>
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[
M = uint8([10:30:70; 20:30:80; 30:30:90]);
R = rms(M, 'native')
% R = uint8([22 51 80])
D = rms(M)
% D = [21.6025 50.6623 80.4156]
]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
